WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.606
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.906 --> 00:00:09.385
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:15.356
Unit nineteen: My Travel Diary. In this unit, you will write about a trip in the past.

4
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.119
Diary.

5
00:00:17.819 --> 00:00:20.399
Diary means a book where you write about your day.

6
00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:22.652
I write in my diary every night.

7
00:00:23.352 --> 00:00:26.097
Your turn. Say: Diary.

8
00:00:28.797 --> 00:00:29.624
Diary.

9
00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:31.211
Trip.

10
00:00:31.911 --> 00:00:34.538
Trip means a short journey to a place and back.

11
00:00:34.838 --> 00:00:36.396
We went on a trip to Kep.

12
00:00:37.096 --> 00:00:39.667
Your turn. Say: Trip.

13
00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:43.020
Trip.

14
00:00:44.017 --> 00:00:44.832
Journey.

15
00:00:45.532 --> 00:00:48.321
Journey means traveling from one place to another.

16
00:00:48.621 --> 00:00:50.737
The bus journey took five hours.

17
00:00:51.437 --> 00:00:53.776
Your turn. Say: Journey.

18
00:00:56.476 --> 00:00:57.302
Journey.

19
00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:59.202
Arrived.

20
00:00:59.902 --> 00:01:02.493
Arrived means came to a place (past of arrive).

21
00:01:02.793 --> 00:01:04.688
We arrived in Siem Reap at noon.

22
00:01:05.388 --> 00:01:07.611
Your turn. Say: Arrived.

23
00:01:10.311 --> 00:01:11.289
Arrived.

24
00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:13.180
Explored.

25
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.982
Explored means looked around a new place (past of explore).

26
00:01:17.282 --> 00:01:19.050
We explored the old temples.

27
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.483
Your turn. Say: Explored.

28
00:01:25.183 --> 00:01:26.126
Explored.

29
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:27.920
Tried.

30
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.280
Tried means did or tasted something for the first time (past of try).

31
00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.603
I tried crab with Kampot pepper.

32
00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:38.013
Your turn. Say: Tried.

33
00:01:40.713 --> 00:01:41.401
Tried.

34
00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:43.313
Amazing.

35
00:01:44.013 --> 00:01:46.628
Amazing means very surprising and wonderful.

36
00:01:46.928 --> 00:01:48.498
The sunset was amazing!

37
00:01:49.198 --> 00:01:51.909
Your turn. Say: Amazing.

38
00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:55.610
Amazing.

39
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:57.595
Memories.

40
00:01:58.295 --> 00:02:00.956
Memories means things you remember from the past.

41
00:02:01.256 --> 00:02:03.267
That trip gave us happy memories.

42
00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:06.480
Your turn. Say: Memories.

43
00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.251
Memories.

44
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.226
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.526 --> 00:02:15.921
Sreypich, where did you go on holiday?

46
00:02:17.217 --> 00:02:18.996
I went to Kep with my family.

47
00:02:20.283 --> 00:02:21.528
What did you do there?

48
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:25.582
We arrived on Friday and explored the crab market.

49
00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:28.360
Did you try anything new?

50
00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:33.733
Yes! I tried crab with Kampot pepper. It was amazing!

51
00:02:35.017 --> 00:02:38.375
Grammar focus: Past simple for a narrative.

52
00:02:38.675 --> 00:02:41.826
First, we arrived in Kep. Then, we explored the market.

53
00:02:42.126 --> 00:02:49.086
Tell a story in order with the past simple. Remember irregular verbs: go → went, see → saw.

54
00:02:50.083 --> 00:02:53.479
Now read and listen. Dear Diary: My Trip to Kep.

55
00:02:53.779 --> 00:02:56.463
Last weekend, my family went on a trip to Kep.

56
00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.085
The journey by car took three hours, and we arrived at lunchtime.

57
00:03:02.383 --> 00:03:05.869
First, we explored the crab market and tried fresh crab with pepper.

58
00:03:07.183 --> 00:03:10.297
Then, we watched an amazing sunset by the sea.

59
00:03:11.583 --> 00:03:14.953
It was a great trip, and I wrote all my memories in my diary.

60
00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.751
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:19.051 --> 00:03:20.958
Last week, we blank to Kep.

62
00:03:21.258 --> 00:03:24.528
A, went. B, go. C, goes.

63
00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:30.087
The answer is A: went.

64
00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:34.047
A book where you write about your day is a blank.

65
00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:37.548
A, diary. B, trip. C, memory.

66
00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.422
The answer is A: diary.

67
00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:47.114
Very surprising and wonderful is blank.

68
00:03:47.414 --> 00:03:50.649
A, amazing. B, tired. C, boring.

69
00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.731
The answer is A: amazing.

70
00:03:58.217 --> 00:04:01.357
Now it's your turn to speak. Tell me about a trip you took.

71
00:04:06.657 --> 00:04:13.854
Last year, I went to Siem Reap. First, we explored Angkor Wat. Then, I tried amok. It was an amazing trip.

72
00:04:14.154 --> 00:04:15.933
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:21.310
Great work today! You learned eight new words and past simple for a narrative.

74
00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:25.389
Today's value is adventure. Try new things and explore safely.

75
00:04:25.689 --> 00:04:28.016
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

76
00:04:28.316 --> 00:04:31.201
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

